"To expand the expression \\((x+3)(2x-6)\\), we use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\n\\[\n(x+3)(2x-6) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-6) + 3 \\cdot 2x + 3 \\cdot (-6)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\nx \\cdot 2x = 2x^2\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\cdot (-6) = -6x\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 2x = 6x\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\cdot (-6) = -18\n\\]\n\nAdding these terms together:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 - 6x + 6x - 18\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 0x - 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x^2 - 18}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(2x^2 - 18\\)."
