"The word MISSISSIPPI has 11 letters, with the letters I and S appearing twice each. To find the number of distinct arrangements, we use the formula for the number of permutations of a word with repeated letters:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{n!}{n_1! \\cdot n_2! \\cdot \\ldots \\cdot n_k!}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the total number of letters, and \\( n_1, n_2, \\ldots, n_k \\) are the frequencies of the distinct letters.\n\nFor MISSISSIPPI:\n- \\( n = 11 \\)\n- \\( n_1 = 2 \\) (for I)\n- \\( n_2 = 2 \\) (for S)\n\nThus, the number of distinct arrangements is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{11!}{2! \\cdot 2!} = \\frac{3991600}{4} = 997900\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word MISSISSIPPI is \\(\\boxed{997900}\\)."
