"To determine the number of ways to divide 10 players into two teams of 5, we can use the concept of combinations. Specifically, we need to choose the number of ways to choose 5 players out of 10 to form the first team, and the remaining 5 players will automatically form the second team.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 5 players out of 10 is given by the combination formula:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{5} = \\frac{10!}{5!(10-5)!} = \\frac{10!}{5! \\cdot 5!}\n\\]\n\nCalculating this, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{5} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7 \\times 6}{5 \\times 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 252\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways ways to divide the 10 players into two teams of 5 is \\(\\boxed{252}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $252$. I hope it is correct."
