"To determine the number of ways to choose 4 books out of 12 without regard to the order, we use the combination formula \\(\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\\), where \\(n\\) is the total number of items, and \\(k\\) is the number of items to choose.\n\nHere, \\(n = 12\\) and \\(k = 4\\).\n\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{4} = \\frac{12!}{4!(12-4)!} = \\frac{12!}{4! \\cdot 8!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{4} = \\frac{12 \\times 11 \\times 10 \\times 9}{4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{1980}{24} = 495\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to choose 4 books out of 12 is \\(\\boxed{495}\\)."
